            <div xml:id="d626">

                <pb facs="0525" n="409" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg409"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 365.117/35.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Ambassador Page to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Rome</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-10-08">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 8, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>38. Your number 30, September 21. War Office requests date and place of birth and
                    parent’s name John Ciappone. Give similar information concerning all other
                    cases.</p>
                <p>Government finds it most difficult to reply officially permitting subjects,
                    naturalization America, to escape military service without granting similar
                    privileges to certain other countries.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Page</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
